From 7ae56009363a9da421666440ff32b2fb87ffbca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:45:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] agentPlugins: route the remaining manifest probes through
 pathExists

Three probes on the agent host still used IFileService.exists(), which
turns a permission failure into false and rejects outright when the
resource's scheme has no provider: the .mcp.json check in the Claude
folder-picker criteria, the manifest check that decides whether a
.claude/skills/<name> directory is a native plugin rather than a
standalone skill, and the manifest check used to resolve an enabled
native plugin's root. An unreadable manifest was therefore treated as
absent without the warning the previous commit introduced, and an
unaddressable working directory made the folder-picker probe and
native plugin resolution reject instead of falling back.

They now go through pathExists with the threaded logger, so a missing
file stays silent and every other failure is warned about and treated
as absent. detectPluginFormat additionally probes plugin.json before
calling readAgentPluginManifest, whose own exists() call would
otherwise reject on a missing provider one line before the probes
above are reached.

createInMemoryFileService in the customization test utilities accepts
a provider so a test can inject failures, and a CapturingLogService
there is shared by the new tests.
